# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in from the Firebase console
# (Project settings -> General -> Your apps -> Web app config).
#
# The whole config object goes in one variable. Paste it however the console
# gives it to you — `const firebaseConfig = { apiKey: "...", ... };` works as-is,
# and so does JSON. Unquoted keys, single quotes, trailing commas, the `const`
# and the semicolon are all fine. Multi-line values need quoting, as below.
#
# These values are NOT secrets: a Firebase web config is shipped to every
# browser by design. Access control lives in firestore.rules, not here.

VITE_FIREBASE_CONFIG={"apiKey":"","authDomain":"","projectId":"","storageBucket":"","messagingSenderId":"","appId":""}

# Straight from the console, which is the easier paste — note the quotes, which
# dotenv needs for a value spanning lines:
#
# VITE_FIREBASE_CONFIG='const firebaseConfig = {
#   apiKey: "AIza...",
#   authDomain: "tally-76406.firebaseapp.com",
#   projectId: "tally-76406",
#   storageBucket: "tally-76406.firebasestorage.app",
#   messagingSenderId: "649041020951",
#   appId: "1:649041020951:web:3c1f..."
# };'

# Domains that serve Tally's *own* Firebase Auth handler, comma-separated.
#
# Leave this empty and Google sign-in still works in a browser tab, but not in
# an installed home-screen app: that case can only use signInWithRedirect, and
# the redirect's handshake is stored against the `authDomain` origin. When that
# is the console default (`tally-76406.firebaseapp.com`) and the app is on your
# own domain, storage partitioning — Safari, every browser on iOS, and Firefox
# — throws the handshake away and sign-in dies with "missing initial state".
#
# Firebase Hosting already answers `/__/auth/*` on every domain attached to the
# site, so the fix is just to name yours here. Tally then points `authDomain`
# at whichever of these it is actually being served from, and leaves the
# console default alone everywhere else (localhost, PR preview channels).
#
# This is opt-in because it cannot be checked from the browser: each domain
# listed must ALSO be registered with Google, or the redirect fails outright
# with `redirect_uri_mismatch`. See docs/deployment-setup.md#the-sign-in-domain.
#
# Set it here rather than editing `authDomain` inside VITE_FIREBASE_CONFIG:
# that field is the fallback for every host NOT on this list, and one build is
# reached at several of them.
#
# VITE_AUTH_DOMAINS=tally.example.org,tally-76406.web.app

# Set to "true" to point the app at the local Firebase Emulator Suite, which
# needs no config above at all. `npm run dev:emulated` sets this for you.
VITE_USE_EMULATORS=false

# Emulator hosts/ports — only read when VITE_USE_EMULATORS=true.
# Defaults match firebase.json, so you normally do not need to set these.
VITE_EMULATOR_HOST=127.0.0.1
VITE_EMULATOR_AUTH_PORT=9099
VITE_EMULATOR_FIRESTORE_PORT=8080
